# Optional environment file for sudharma-pool.service
# Copy to /etc/sudharma/pool.env and adjust before enabling the service.
#
# Primary pool configuration lives in /etc/sudharma/pool.json
# (installed from deployment/testnet/pool.example.json). The systemd unit
# loads this file with EnvironmentFile=- so it is safe to omit until needed.
#
# Example pool.json fields:
#   rpc_url, payout_address, payout_scheme (pps|pplns|solo|fpps),
#   pool_difficulty, stratum_listen, work_poll_seconds
#
# Remote binary upgrade (manual operator action):
# SUDHARMA_POOL_BIN_URL=https://example.com/sudharma-pool-linux-amd64
# SUDHARMA_POOL_INSTALL_PATH=/usr/local/bin/sudharma-pool
# SUDHARMA_POOL_CONFIG=/etc/sudharma/pool.json
# SUDHARMA_POOL_SERVICE=sudharma-pool
#
# Probe mining RPC before enabling the service:
#   sudharma-pool -config /etc/sudharma/pool.json -probe
#   go run ./cmd/sudharma-mining-readiness
